{"text": "OFFICE OF THE GOVERNOR\n\nJanuary 6, 2020\n\nVia Electronic Mail\n\nMax Lu\n84895-04966634@requests.muckrock.com\n\nRE: Public Records Act Request\nDear Mr. Lu:\n\nThis letter is in response to your correspondence to the Governor's Office received\nJanuary 2, 2020 requesting \u201ccopies of all email exchanges and documents regarding Governor\nBrown\u2019s 2017 trip to China, such as:\n\u00a9 list of accompanying government officials and their email exchanges regarding this trip\nto China\nMeeting schedules in China and how are they set up\nGovernor Brown's unusual meeting with China's President Xi Jinping (normally, a\nnational-level official will not meet with state-level officials directly). Who proposed this,\nmeeting and how did it happen?\n\u2018\u00a9 meeting memos\u201d\n\nPlease be advised that we are not the custodian of records from the Brown\nAdministration. You may wish to contact the California State Archives:\n\n1020 O Street\nSacramento, CA 95814\n(916) 653-7715\nOtherwise, we have found no records responsive to your request.\n\nSincerely,\n\nPour O\u2014\n\nDAvID Sapp\nDeputy Legal Affairs Secretary\n\nGOVERNOR GAVIN NEWSOM + SACRAMENTO, CA 95814 + (916) 445-2841\n=",
